      'Blood is made of plasma, the fluid part, which accounts for about 55% of its volume, and cells, which make up the rest. Plasma is mostly water, with dissolved proteins (including antibodies and complement), salts and nutrients. The cells are the red blood cells, which carry oxygen, the platelets, which help blood clot, and the white blood cells, which defend the body.',
